  "note": "Two current-build analysis workers compare knnCache:false versus true, with separate source clouds and pools. An archived pre-change build supplies one untimed full-output oracle per method, then terminates before timing. Every pair checks all normal f32 bits or kept count and byte-identical SOR PLY against both the fresh current build and archived output. Full unchanged measured input, k=24, normals up, SOR ratio=1. Pool startup/loading excluded. One excluded first-use pair per method, five excluded alternating warm-up pairs, ten alternating timed pairs unless overridden. First-use samples are not cold medians. Whole RPC includes native search/PCA/filter, partition/tree/order construction as applicable, messages, joins, output copies, SOR filtered-cloud indexing. Cache diagnostics/verification/exports/result removal outside timing. Fresh controls must retain no preparation; prepared controls must reuse the same group, with exact incremental reuse counts and actual retained capacities plus root index/region bytes at most 128 MiB. Parameters/results not cached. Eligibility uses a conservative preallocation estimate; native capacity checks follow preparation. One idle source group plus leased in-flight groups; this is not a total process-memory cap. No builds/tests/scans run during timing. Input/manifest/source/script/both-build artifact hashes checked before/after. CPU clocks/power/GC/other apps uncontrolled. Measured subsets are not independent surveys or ground truth. No GPU metadata collected."
